course: dictionary
lesson: 14274
title: Nodule: a small round lump
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A nodule is a small, round lump. It can be on a body, on a plant root, or in a rock. The word has a clue in it: a nodule is a little knot or bump. «Pea plants have tiny nodules on their roots» tells you the nodules are on the roots, and they are small and round.
explain: Look at the words around the word. «The doctor felt a small nodule on her neck and checked it carefully.» Small tells you the lump is not big, and the doctor checking it tells you it is something a doctor needs to look at. You can work out the meaning from the clues.
explain: Scientists use the word in different subjects. «Hunters found a flint nodule in the chalk cliff.» Here the nodule is a lump inside a rock. Think about where the word is used, then swap in your meaning, "a small round lump", and check it still makes sense.
fact: A nodule is a small, round lump.
fact: A nodule can be on the body, on a plant root, or in a rock.
fact: In peas, beans and clover, root nodules hold bacteria that take nitrogen from the air and feed the plant.
fact: Flint often forms as nodules in chalk rock.
fact: Nodule is said NOD-yool.
exercise: «Pea plants have tiny nodules on their roots.» What is a nodule? | A deep hole in the ground | *A small round lump | A long thin stem | A kind of seed
exercise: «The doctor felt a small nodule on her neck and checked it carefully.» What did the doctor do? | Left the room quickly | *Checked the small lump carefully | Cooked a meal | Painted the wall
exercise: «Hunters found a flint nodule in the chalk cliff.» Find and copy the word that names a kind of stone found in chalk. | found | *flint | hunters | cliff
test: Root nodules on beans hold bacteria. What do the bacteria do for the plant? | Make the roots dry | Stop the plant from growing | *Take nitrogen from the air and feed the plant | Paint the leaves
test: Nadia says a nodule is a big flat sheet. What is the right meaning? | A long, thin wire | A loud noise | A big flat sheet | *A small round lump
exam: «The rock held a dark nodule the size of a pea.» What does nodule mean here? | A bright light | A loud crack | A large flat sheet | *A small round lump
